  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong dark editorial style, disciplined cyan/red/yellow semantics, and consistent cards across viewports. However, desktop composition is top-heavy with a large dead zone beside the headline and an undersized explanatory callout; tablet/mobile become dense and vertically repetitive. Small, low-contrast mono labels and body copy reduce legibility. The desktop header’s oversized cropped background lettering is distracting, while tablet/mobile navigation visibly truncates labels and makes the information architecture feel unfinished.",
    "fix": "Rebalance the desktop hero into a deliberate two-column composition, enlarge and brighten supporting copy, reduce mobile card padding/vertical repetition, and establish a clearer responsive header pattern with an explicit menu or stronger scroll affordance instead of clipped navigation.",
